{"relationshipsSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SK","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sl","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8CopyableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s23CustomStringConvertibleP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SQ","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s9EscapableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s25ExpressibleByArrayLiteralP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/SH","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/Sk","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s8SendableP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/s16SendableMetatypeP","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/ST"],"kind":"relationships","title":"Conforms To","type":"conformsTo"}],"primaryContentSections":[{"kind":"declarations","declarations":[{"tokens":[{"text":"@frozen","kind":"attribute"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"struct","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"LazySegmentTree","kind":"identifier"},{"text":"<","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"genericParameter"},{"text":"> ","kind":"text"},{"text":"where","kind":"keyword"},{"text":" ","kind":"text"},{"text":"Action","kind":"typeIdentifier"},{"text":" : ","kind":"text"},{"text":"MonoidAction","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","kind":"typeIdentifier","preciseIdentifier":"s:10RangeTrees12MonoidActionP"}],"languages":["swift"],"platforms":["Linux"]}]},{"content":[{"text":"Overview","anchor":"overview","type":"heading","level":2},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The layout is "},{"type":"reference","identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/SegmentTree","isActive":true},{"type":"text","text":"‘s: a perfect binary tree over the values padded to a power of"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"two, in one flat array of cells. Beside each internal cell sits a pending update, applied to"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"that cell’s value but not yet to the cells below it. A range update applies itself to the"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"O(log "},{"type":"emphasis","inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"n"}]},{"type":"text","text":") cells that cover the range and leaves it pending there, pushing older pending"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"updates down one level on the way so that updates reach each cell in the order they were made."},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"A query reads without changing the tree, composing the pending updates of the cells it"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"passes through."}],"type":"paragraph"},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"The "},{"identifier":"doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/MonoidAction","isActive":true,"type":"reference"},{"type":"text","text":" names the monoid and the updates:"}],"type":"paragraph"},{"syntax":"swift","type":"codeListing","code":["enum AddToSum: MonoidAction {","    typealias Values = Sum<Int>","    static var identity: Int { 0 }","    static func compose(_ outer: Int, _ inner: Int) -> Int { outer + inner }","    static func apply(_ update: Int, to sum: Int, count: Int) -> Int { sum + update * count }","}","","var tree = LazySegmentTree<AddToSum>([1, 2, 3, 4, 5])","tree.apply(10, in: 1 ..< 4)","tree.combined(in: 0 ..< 5)   \/\/ 45","tree[2]                      \/\/ 13"]},{"inlineContent":[{"type":"text","text":"As a collection, a lazy segment tree’s elements are the values, in order, with every update"},{"type":"text","text":" "},{"type":"text","text":"applied."}],"type":"paragraph"}],"kind":"content"}],"sections":[],"topicSections":[{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/init()","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/init(_:)"],"generated":true,"title":"Initializers","anchor":"Initializers"},{"identifiers":["doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/apply(_:checkedIn:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/apply(_:in:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegmentTree\/combined(checkedIn:)","doc:\/\/RangeTrees\/documentation\/RangeTrees\/LazySegm